#	-g	1
v	live	Display the settings currently in use. (default if no argument given)
v	custom	Display custom settings for all power sources
v	cap	Display which power management features the machine supports
v	sched	Display scheduled startup/wake and shutdown/sleep events
v	ups	Display UPS emergency thresholds
v	ps	Display status of batteries and UPSs
v	batt	Display status of batteries and UPSs
v	pslog	Display an ongoing log of power source (battery and UPS)state
v	rawlog	Display an ongoing log of battery state as read directly from battery
v	profiles	Display the settings associated with each Energy Saver profile. 10.5+
v	thermlog	Show a log of thermal notifications that affect CPU speed. Not available on all platforms
v	assertions	Display a summary of power assertions. 10.6+
v	assertionslog	Show a log of assertion creations and releases. 10.6+
v	activity	Display a summary of power state of Display wrangler and Disk Queue Manager.10.6+
v	activitylog	Show a log of power state changes to Display Wrangler and Disk Queue Manager. 10.6+
v	sysload	Display the "system load advisory" 10.6+
v	sysloadlog	Display an ongoing log of lives changes to the system load advisory. 10.6+
v	ac	Display details about an attached AC power adapter
v	adapter	Display details about an attached AC power adapter
v	log	Display a history of sleeps, wakes, and other power management events
v	uuid	Display the currently active sleep/wake UUID
v	uuidlog	Display the currently active sleep/wake UUID, and prints a new UUID as they're set by the system
v	history	A debugging tool. Prints a timeline of system sleeplwake UUIDs
v	historydetailed	Prints driver-level timings for a sleep/wake. Pass a UUID as an argument
v	everything	Print output from every argument under the GETTING header 10.8+
